//! s251 (wolf-lang#806; yew's `term.render_new_env` twin): a one-line
//! module function that makes a closure and calls another function
//! with it, IMPORTED into the entry's cluster and inlined there by the
//! release tier's cross-cluster round. The ballast, called under a
//! loop so its edges weigh more than `render_env`'s, fills the entry's
//! cluster to the target size before the `render_env` edge is
//! considered; `tty.render_env` and its closure's entry
//! `tty.render_env.cls0` land in the other cluster. The import
//! decision then brings `render_env`'s body across (it is small and
//! single-use), the inliner splices it into `main`, and the entry's
//! object builds the static record of an entry it does not own: at
//! 808ce11a `a vtable slot @tty.render_env.cls0 outside this object's
